From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mtbl23 <mbhangal23@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:12:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Gale port: skip the planar speed factor multiplication when
 the factor is exactly 1

Entity#move multiplied the delta movement by the block speed factor (a new Vec3
and a setDeltaMovement call) even for the usual factor of 1.0. Multiplying by
exactly 1.0 returns the same components, so the multiplication is skipped for
that case only. Leaf's tolerance based variant (1e-6) is not ported because it
is not bit identical.

Adapted from Leaf "Skip negligible planar movement multiplication" by Martijn
Muijsers, Gale (GPL-3.0-only). Leaf: https://github.com/Winds-Studio/Leaf

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
index 9276c4ed78442a3cb6f9018655249dc31091b0d2..13d79d75614dbc55e418862f321cc4308b400602 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
@@ -1293,7 +1293,11 @@ public abstract class Entity
                 }
 
                 float blockSpeedFactor = this.getBlockSpeedFactor();
-                this.setDeltaMovement(this.getDeltaMovement().multiply(blockSpeedFactor, 1.0, blockSpeedFactor));
+                // Leaf port start - multiplying by exactly 1.0 returns the same components (also for -0.0 and NaN), so skip the new Vec3 and the movement hook (Leaf "Skip negligible planar movement multiplication", Martijn Muijsers, Gale; GPL-3.0-only, the exact-one case only)
+                if (blockSpeedFactor != 1.0F) {
+                    this.setDeltaMovement(this.getDeltaMovement().multiply(blockSpeedFactor, 1.0, blockSpeedFactor));
+                }
+                // Leaf port end
                 profiler.pop();
             }
         }
